LibreEfficientNetV2 — third-party attribution
=============================================

The EfficientNetV2 architecture in this family (``nn.py``) is a native
re-implementation derived from the EfficientNet/EfficientNetV2 implementation
in `timm` (PyTorch Image Models):

    Source:   https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
    Files:    timm/models/efficientnet.py, timm/models/_efficientnet_blocks.py,
              timm/models/_efficientnet_builder.py
    Author:   Ross Wightman and the timm contributors
    License:  Apache License 2.0

The original architecture is from Google:

    EfficientNetV2 — "EfficientNetV2: Smaller Models and Faster Training"
    (https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.00298), reference implementation
    https://github.com/google/automl/tree/master/efficientnetv2
    License:  Apache License 2.0

The block definitions, per-variant architecture strings, channel-rounding,
TensorFlow "SAME" padding, and module/attribute naming follow timm so that
timm's Apache-2.0 ImageNet-1k pretrained weights load unchanged and produce
bit-identical inference output (verified by the parity test).

Pretrained weights (tf_efficientnetv2_b{0,1,2,3}, ImageNet-1k, ported by
Ross Wightman in timm — no ImageNet-21k, no JFT, no extra data) are licensed
Apache-2.0 and are redistributable for commercial use.

